<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Limits of Polynomials — direct substitution</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Evaluate the limit</p>
<p>\[ \lim_{x \to {@aa@}} \left( {@fx@} \right). \]</p>
<div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A polynomial is <strong>continuous</strong> everywhere, so its limit as \(x \to a\) is just its value at \(a\). The limit is found by <strong>direct substitution</strong>; no special limit technique is needed.</p>
\[ \lim_{x \to {@aa@}}\left({@fx@}\right) = {@p@}\times({@aa@})^2 + {@q@}\times({@aa@}) + {@r@} = {@p*aa^2@} - {@-q*aa@} + {@r@} = {@ta@}. \]
<p>Watch the signs: \(({@aa@})^2 = {@aa^2@}\) is positive, while \({@q@}\times({@aa@})\) is negative.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2026063000</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text>p: rand_with_prohib(1,5,[]);
q: rand_with_prohib(1,9,[]);
aa: -rand_with_prohib(2,6,[]);
/* r is chosen so that the limit is never 0, 1 or -1 (trivial answers) */
r0: -(p*aa^2 + q*aa);
r: rand_with_prohib(1,9,[r0, r0+1, r0-1]);
fx: p*x^2 + q*x + r;
ta: subst(x=aa, fx);
/* Diagnostics, always distinct from ta and from each other (checked over the domain):
   the square of a negative taken as negative; the negative x-value substituted as positive. */
wrong_sign: -p*aa^2 + q*aa + r;
wrong_abs: p*aa^2 - q*aa + r;</text>
    </questionvariables>
    <specificfeedback format="html">
      <text>[[feedback:prt1]]</text>
    </specificfeedback>
    <questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[lim x -> {@aa@} of {@fx@} = {@ta@}]]></text>
    </questionnote>
    <questiondescription format="html">
